{
  "manufacturer": "Systemair",
  "manufacturer_slug": "systemair",
  "model": "SYS GW IMS BAC(A) VRF BACnet gateway",
  "model_slug": "sys-gw-ims-bac-a",
  "aliases": [
    "SYS GW IMS BAC(A)",
    "SYS GW IMS BAC",
    "IMMP-BAC(A)",
    "IMMP-BAC",
    "Systemair VRF BACnet gateway",
    "SYS GW gateway"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "VRF BACnet IP gateway",
  "applies_to": "Systemair SYSVRF indoor units, outdoor units and high-temperature hydro modules (HTHM) on the outdoor unit X/Y/E bus.",
  "summary": "The SYS GW IMS BAC(A) gateway (IMMP-BAC(A) in the manual) links Systemair VRF systems to a BMS over BACnet IP. It has four RS-485 ports to the outdoor units' X/Y/E bus (up to 64 indoor units per port, 384 indoor and outdoor units in total) and one Ethernet port. Each indoor unit, outdoor unit and HTHM appears as its own BACnet device with fixed object instances, so one template per unit type covers the site. Indoor units take on/off, mode, fan speed, setpoint and swing commands; outdoor units are monitoring only.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet IP"
  ],
  "firmware": null,
  "default_device_instance": null,
  "access_inferred": false,
  "notes": [
    "Device instance per unit: indoor = network number × 10000 + port × 1000 + indoor address (0-63); outdoor = network number × 10000 + port × 1000 + 100 + outdoor address (0-31). Port 0-3; port 0 is the RS-485 port next to the Ethernet port. The manual gives no separate rule for HTHM units (AI 11 lists HTHM as indoor unit type 17).",
    "The list holds three object sets: indoor unit devices, outdoor unit devices and HTHM devices. Instances repeat between indoor and outdoor devices (AI 1, AI 7-14, BI 2 and BV 1 mean different things).",
    "Error code values (indoor AI 7, outdoor AI 8, HTHM AV 63): 0 = no error; then blocks of 20 per letter, 1-20 = A0-AF, AH, AL, AP, AU; 21-40 = b; 41-60 = C; 61-80 = E; 81-100 = F; 101-120 = H; 121-140 = L; 141-160 = J; 161-180 = n; 181-200 = P; 201-220 = r; 221-240 = t; 241-260 = U. The unit's service manual gives the meaning.",
    "The manual's HTHM table prints AV 70 (EXV 1) twice; it is listed once here.",
    "Not every indoor model supports every object; cooling-only systems do not support auto or heat modes."
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "Operation and Installation Manual - IMMP-BAC(A) Manual",
    "doc_number": null,
    "revision_date": null,
    "url": "https://stepimassets.blob.core.windows.net/dsassetsprod/IOM_BACNET_GATEWAY_GB.PDF"
  },
  "integration": {
    "summary": "Wire each RS-485 port to an outdoor unit's X/Y/E bus, set the gateway's IP address and a unique BACnet network number on its web page, restart it, then discover the per-unit BACnet devices. Map each indoor unit's on/off, mode, fan speed and setpoint commands plus room temperature and alarm. Outdoor unit devices are for monitoring; HTHM devices have their own heating and water-heating on/off commands and setpoints (BV 90/91, AV 50/51).",
    "minimum_points": [
      {
        "ref": "BV 1",
        "name": "On/Off Setting",
        "why": "Start/stop indoor unit"
      },
      {
        "ref": "MV 1",
        "name": "Mode Setting",
        "why": "Mode command (3 = cool, 4 = heat, 5 = auto)"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 1",
        "name": "Temperature Setting",
        "why": "Setpoint command, 10-30 °C"
      },
      {
        "ref": "MV 2",
        "name": "Fan Speed Setting",
        "why": "Fan speed command (8 = auto)"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 1",
        "name": "Room Temperature",
        "why": "Indoor unit room temperature"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BI 2",
        "name": "Alarm Indication",
        "why": "Indoor unit has an error code"
      }
    ],
    "enable": "No enable point is documented. Writing BV 1 on starts the indoor unit with its last-used mode, fan speed and setpoint; if the unit was off when the gateway first came online it defaults to cooling at 24 °C, low fan. Locks (BV 4, BV 5, MV 3, MV 5) restrict local changes.",
    "heartbeat": null,
    "remote_sensors": null,
    "setup": [
      "Factory IP address 192.168.1.8; set the IP, BACnet network number, date and admin password from a web browser (default admin login is in the manual).",
      "BACnet network number 2-254: each gateway needs a different one, not used by any other device; restart after changing it.",
      "Device instance = network number × 10000 + port × 1000 + unit address (+ 100 for outdoor units).",
      "The gateway must be on the same IP subnet as the BMS head end.",
      "Power is 24 VAC; the gateway clips onto the supplied mounting rail.",
      "The PICS page ticks only ISO 8802-3 (10BASE-T) as the data link, but the manual describes the Ethernet port as connecting to a BACnet/IP network."
    ],
    "gotchas": [
      "Space commands at least 200 ms apart; commands sent faster can be lost.",
      "Instances are not unique across unit types: indoor and outdoor devices reuse AI 1, AI 7-14, BI 2 and BV 1.",
      "Fan speed value 9 (off) is status only; it cannot be written.",
      "In auto mode the cooling setpoint (AV 2) must be at or above the heating setpoint (AV 3), or the gateway may change it to match.",
      "Outdoor BV 1 Emergency Stop is read only.",
      "All temperatures are in °C."
    ]
  },
